.TH ROBOTEST-SUPERVISOR 8 "August 2026" "robotest-supervisor 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
robotest-supervisor \- bounded local process supervisor for RoboTest Lab
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robotest-supervisor
.RB [ \-config
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-check-config ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B robotest-supervisor
starts configured child process groups, monitors timestamped heartbeat files,
and applies a bounded exponential-backoff restart policy. It writes structured
events and an atomic status snapshot under its configured state directory.
.PP
The HTTP interface is read-only and binds exactly to 127.0.0.1. It exposes
.BR /healthz ,
.BR /readyz ,
.BR /v1/status ,
and
.BR /metrics .
There is no remote process-control endpoint.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Read the strict versioned JSON configuration from
.IR path .
The default is
.IR /etc/robotest-supervisor/config.json .
.TP
.B \-check-config
Validate the configuration and exit without starting a child or HTTP server.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/robotest-supervisor/config.json
Administrator configuration managed as a dpkg conffile.
.TP
.I /var/lib/robotest-supervisor/events.jsonl
Prefix-retained structured lifecycle events.
.TP
.I /var/lib/robotest-supervisor/status.json
Atomically replaced current status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.service (5)
